			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Logging module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and documentation cleanup to the `Source/Logging/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting struct fields within `LogRotationConfig`, `LogContext`, and `SensitiveDataConfig` from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `max_file_size_bytes` -> `MaxFileSizeBytes`, `enabled` -> `Enabled`).\n- Converting local variables and function parameters throughout the module to `PascalCase` (e.g., `request_id` -> `RequestId` in `LogContext::New`, `log_path` -> `log_path` in `ContextLogger::Initialize`).\n- Cleaning up documentation comments to use relative project paths (e.g., `vs/base/common/errors`) instead of absolute file system paths.\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `:u64` instead of `: u64`) and reordering imports for consistency.\n\nThis ensures the `Logging` module, responsible for structured logging, request ID propagation, and log rotation within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "fcc7b98c5ff15f30d492c892cf84419a8120e7f6"
