			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Library module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and variable naming normalization to the `Source/Library.rs` file, the central aggregation point for the Air daemon's exports, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting function parameters and local variables in the `utils` module from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `path` -> `Path`, `prefix` -> `Prefix`, `attempt` -> `Attempt`).\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations in constant definitions (e.g., `&str:` instead of `&str :`).\n- Collapsing simple `From` trait implementations into single-line blocks for conciseness.\n- Reorganizing `pub use` exports for better alphabetical grouping.\n- Adding the `windows_subsystem = \"windows\"` attribute for release builds.\n\nThis ensures the `Library` module, responsible for exposing the core `AirError` types, constants, and utility functions, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
