			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Indexing module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and documentation cleanup to the `Source/Indexing/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` within the `IndexFileInternal` method and related helper functions (e.g., `Metadata`, `Content`, `Checksum`).\n- Updating struct field access and function call arguments to reflect the capitalized naming convention.\n- Cleaning up documentation comments to use relative project paths (e.g., `vs/workbench/services/search`) instead of absolute file system paths.\n- Adjusting whitespace and indentation for consistent formatting across the module.\n\nThis ensures the `Indexing` module, responsible for file search, content analysis, and symbol extraction within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
