			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in HealthCheck module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization and documentation cleanup to the `Source/HealthCheck/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `start_time` -> `StartTime`, `response_time` -> `ResponseTime`).\n- Updating utility function calls to reflect PascalCase naming (e.g., `utils::current_timestamp()` -> `utils::CurrentTimestamp()`).\n- Cleaning up documentation comments to use relative project paths instead of absolute file system paths.\n\nThis ensures the `HealthCheck` module, responsible for monitoring service status, performance metrics, and resource utilization within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
