			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Downloader module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization to the `Source/Downloader/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `sanitized_url` -> `SanitizedUrl`, `download_id` -> `DownloadId`, `destination` -> `Destination`).\n- Updating utility function calls to reflect PascalCase naming (e.g., `utils::generate_request_id()` -> `utils::GenerateRequestId()`, `utils::validate_file_path` -> `utils::ValidateFilePath`).\n- Modifying struct field initializations and error handling variables to align with the capitalized naming convention.\n\nThis ensures the `Downloader` module, responsible for managing asynchronous file transfers and resilience logic within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
